  "regression_evidence": [
    "Reservations and the indexed owner binding commit with the job attempt. A rolled-back reservation is absent; cross-owner request claims are rejected.",
    "Three invalid-rubric attempts retain all three metered charges; the retry subtotal is included in the total. Exhaustion, supersession and mode Off do not remove costs.",
    "Source deletion removes the original job but retained content-free cost metadata preserves owner/session/request charges and identifies the subset without job details.",
    "A two-hop fallback exposes the known final-hop estimate while leaving the complete cost unknown. A terminal rejection before any upstream hop proves zero.",
    "A successful cached/completed job retry issues no new model request. Duplicate IDs are rejected before auth and preserve existing metering.",
    "Missing usage remains unknown despite the legacy numeric zero column. A confirmed no-charge receipt resolves it to zero.",
    "A pending receipt makes the total incomplete while preserving its provisional metered amount. An authoritative receipt refreshes the amount without changing the assessment count or issuing another request.",
    "Cancelled in-flight work retains its request identity and unknown total when a fresh cost reader inspects the same database.",
    "The local IPC/TUI inspector explicitly labels a zero known subtotal with missing dispatch/metering as an unknown total and makes no net-savings claim."
  ],
